{
  "version": 1,
  "provenance": {
    "language_slots": "Thirty native EU-only arrays each contain five language-selected pointers. Bounds come from the five-language domain and distinct roots in poo,allmap,title,status,mode_worldwarp,mode_ms,mode_ms2,ms_charge and mode_mapinspect. These are runtime locale selectors, not encoded assets. There are no US/JP counterpart definitions or interpolated spans.",
    "table_targets": "Nested title/status/resource selectors use void**[5], and the map-inspect animation selector uses AnimHeader**[5]. Every nested target is a separately source-owned real array (actor_ui_resource_data,remaining_resource_data or animation_resource_data), never a byte-view alias. status.c explicitly selects gfx0,1,2 from the EC8 family and GetMaxSpriteTileBytes(...,4) bounds the F08 family. Title uses three gfx slots; room/map-inspect tables have independent animation frame bounds. Existing raw encoded-asset bindings are reused when available; remaining native tile/map/Sprite labels point to original payloads and are not counted as C-owned data.",
    "direct_consumers": "Two Pooh u8-pointer selectors supply floor-indexed0x140-byte graphics. Allmap and shop map selectors feed LoadBgMap/RequestTilemapRectCopy. Status selectors feed LoadObjTiles,DrawSprite and counted graphics arrays. Worldwarp and mode_ms2 direct Sprite selectors feed DrawSprite; each of their45 pointed-to Sprite streams independently parses to its complete2+6*count byte extent. Existing raw references and region guards remain unchanged except removing now-canonical TU-local extern declarations."
  },
